# France at war with England: a French Dragoon attacks twice, the English answer on their turns.
# Start: turns_spring_1600_events' output (France, Spring 1600, turn 108; England already at war with
# France) re-saved once; fixture: every French unit with no orders / go-to / pioneer job on sentry,
# except Quebec's Dragoon (unit 131, Veteran Soldier, was fortifying), given no orders and full moves
# and made the active unit (head.active_unit 131, map cursor 45,24).
# Turn 108: the Dragoon attacks the fortified English Dragoon on (45,23): it is routed and demoted to
# Soldiers. England's turn: they beat the colonists near Guadeloupe, capture the wagon train and the
# colonists and march into Guadeloupe (captured: owner -> England, 90 gold plundered).
# Turn 109: the Dragoon attacks the same unit again (Soldiers routed -> Colonists). An attack opens no
# talk (FUN_465b_0000 jumps to LAB_465b_0bd1 past FUN_5bfb_3180, raw 75686-75693); on its turn England
# steps beside Quebec, opens talks and offers a demarcation treaty, refused ("No": @WARMEEK, still at
# war), then beats the French Pioneers near Guadeloupe. Outcomes are fixed by the replayed RNG.
key KP_8                 # turn 108: Dragoon attacks north (45,23)
wait 6
key Return               # combat popups (nested in the attack): English Dragoons routed, demoted to Soldiers
wait 6
key Return               # French defeat English Dragoons near Quebec
wait 6
key Return
wait 6
key space                # end turn 108
wait 30
